  "final_message": "{\"summary\":\"Implemented `safeUploadPath` with strict single-component validation, rejecting traversal, absolute/drive-qualified names, `/` and `\\\\`, empty values, NUL bytes, and non-string filenames. Study Note: this function validates an untrusted upload filename and returns a lexically contained absolute path without filesystem access; previously it always threw. It now uses `path.resolve` plus `path.relative` for containment. Truth status: verified.\",\"files_changed\":[\"src/upload-path.mjs\"],\"tests_run\":[\"`node --test` — 1 passed, 0 failed\",\"Focused security matrix — valid filenames accepted; traversal, absolute/drive paths, separators, empty input, NUL bytes, and non-string values rejected\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[\"Symlink-safe file creation remains intentionally outside this function; downstream storage must use no-follow or equivalent exclusive-open semantics.\",\"No meaningful implementation tasks remain.\"]}",
